Short interpretation
The interactive figures provide the values used in the report comparisons. They do not replace the Korean report.
Most comparisons require three safeguards:

separate total citation counts from citations per DOI-citing policy document;
separate citations to Korean research from citations made by Korean policy documents;
check whether the denominator changes before comparing percentages.

Verification without licensed source data
The public verification script recomputes:

the combined U.S., IGO, and U.K. policy-source share for citations to Korean research;
the U.S. research share cited by Korean policy documents;
the social- and health-science shares in the two Korea-related directions;
Korea’s social-science share gap, its source-type composition and within-source-type components;
the combined KDI-KIEP share, the think-tank shares in both directions, and Korea’s rank among the 11-country field-gap comparison;
think-tank citation shares and top-two institution concentration across the 11 comparison countries;
the social-science distribution of 748 eligible foreign think tanks across 74 countries and the positions of KDI and KIEP;
the country count of the top 25 foreign KDI/KIEP citation-profile matches;
the 36.1% U.S. linked-sample composition expected share;
baseline counts used in the author-country sensitivity analysis;
overall, institution-stratified, and domain-stratified country-assignment missingness and the 40.1%-67.4% mechanical U.S. bounds;
weighting sensitivity of the Korea social-science gap (32.2-59.9 percentage points);
KDI-KIEP document shares, citation share, and citations per DOI-citing document; and
whether the country-domain cache matches the sequential country-assignment rule and the recorded parquet size and modification time.

Extract both archives into the same directory and run:
python scripts/verify_public_report_aggregates.py --root . --run-tag 20251026
A successful run ends with PUBLIC_AGGREGATE_VERIFICATION=PASS. This means the listed values and calculation relationships were confirmed from the public aggregate layer; it does not recreate licensed Overton source records or verify the upstream Overton export universe.
